{"id": "dream-keeper-grant-presidents-firm", "title": "A Dream Keeper grant of $962,500; the charity paid its President’s firm $783,523", "seconds": 167.3, "voice": "elevenlabs:iPYqcpY8j8Ap4jUf28I3", "narrator": "Michael", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "193b530924058320", "words": 412, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]", "actors[0]"], "text": "The Dream Keeper Initiative is the Human Rights Commission’s grant program for Black San Franciscans.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.76, "shot": "d0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Dream Keeper Initiative", "kicker": "Human Rights Commission", "sub": "grants for Black San Franciscans"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.4, 0.67, 1.36, 1.51, 1.61, 1.83, 2.05, 2.51, 2.8, 3.25, 3.4, 3.68, 3.87]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["established[0]", "suspicious[3]", "story[0]"], "text": "Its largest technical-assistance agreement went to a small Berkeley charity, Black Female Project.", "t0": 4.88, "t1": 11.04, "shot": "d1", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Human Rights Commission", "sub": "Dream Keeper technical assistance"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Black Female Project", "sub": "a small Berkeley charity, agreement 1000024180"}], "kicker": "The largest of 16 agreements"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.71, 1.54, 2.1, 2.29, 2.4, 2.48, 2.94, 3.3, 4.16, 4.63, 5.06]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["established[0]", "suspicious[3]", "story[0]"], "text": "How much?", "t0": 11.04, "t1": 12.72, "shot": "d1", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Human Rights Commission", "sub": "Dream Keeper technical assistance"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Black Female Project", "sub": "a small Berkeley charity, agreement 1000024180"}], "kicker": "The largest of 16 agreements"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.26]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "established[0]"], "text": "962,500 dollars.", "t0": 12.72, "t1": 15.84, "shot": "d2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$962,500", "label": "paid by the Human Rights Commission, fiscal 2022 to 2024", "sub": "the largest of 16 Dream Keeper technical-assistance agreements"}, "emph": ["962,500"], "wt": [0.04, 0.38, 0.79, 1.35, 1.9, 2.23, 2.56]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 16.36, "t1": 18.03, "shot": "d3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.33, 0.4, 0.99, 1.17, 1.24]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "story[1]"], "text": "The first lead. The charity’s largest contractor was PJS Consultants, paid for communications.", "t0": 18.25, "t1": 25.07, "shot": "d4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "PJS Consultants", "kicker": "The first lead", "sub": "the charity’s largest contractor, paid for communications"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.74, 2.01, 2.16, 2.59, 3.0, 3.53, 3.72, 4.34, 5.52, 5.82, 5.94]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "PJS gave the same Shattuck Avenue suite the charity gives as its own address.", "t0": 25.19, "t1": 29.49, "shot": "d5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Shattuck Avenue, Berkeley", "kicker": "One address", "sub": "the charity’s own suite, and PJS Consultants"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.61, 0.83, 0.95, 1.31, 1.65, 1.95, 2.29, 2.42, 2.82, 3.27, 3.46, 3.61, 3.78]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[2]", "links[2]"], "text": "And the 2023 return names the principal of PJS: the charity’s President.", "t0": 29.61, "t1": 34.64, "shot": "d6", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "bf3", "kicker": "Form 990 for 2023: insider deals", "text": "the charity’s President is the principal of PJS", "mark": "President"}, "emph": ["President"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.25, 0.6, 1.19, 1.61, 1.96, 2.09, 2.59, 2.68, 3.85, 4.02, 4.53]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[1]"], "text": "Over three years, how much did the charity pay her firm?", "t0": 34.76, "t1": 39.3, "shot": "d7", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Paid to PJS Consultants, by year", "rows": [["2022", "$290,210"], ["2023", "$345,317"], ["2024", "$147,996"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.62, 1.57, 1.82, 2.17, 2.32, 2.41, 2.79, 3.05, 3.2]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "links[1]"], "text": "783,523 dollars.", "t0": 39.3, "t1": 43.94, "shot": "d8", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$783,523", "label": "paid to PJS Consultants, 2022 to 2024", "sub": "at the charity’s own suite"}, "emph": ["783,523"], "wt": [0.04, 0.42, 0.96, 1.6, 2.48, 2.84, 3.28, 4.07]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "timeline[1]"], "text": "The second lead. The 2022 return asks: any business with an officer’s company?", "t0": 44.56, "t1": 51.5, "shot": "d10", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "bf2", "kicker": "Form 990 for 2022, Part IV line 28c", "text": "Return for 2022 filed: PJS Consultants paid $290,210; no business with an officer’s company reported.", "mark": "no business"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.55, 1.49, 1.67, 1.99, 2.48, 3.25, 4.71, 4.94, 5.3, 5.45, 5.53, 5.88]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "timeline[1]"], "text": "It answered no,", "t0": 51.5, "t1": 53.17, "shot": "d11", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["2022 return: business with an officer’s company?", "No"], "b": ["paid to PJS Consultants, 2022", "$290,210"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["no"], "wt": [0.04, 0.23, 0.67]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "timeline[1]"], "text": "while listing 290,210 dollars paid to PJS.", "t0": 53.17, "t1": 58.66, "shot": "d11", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["2022 return: business with an officer’s company?", "No"], "b": ["paid to PJS Consultants, 2022", "$290,210"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.04, 0.31, 0.75, 1.07, 1.46, 1.88, 2.67, 3.01, 3.35, 3.64, 4.4, 4.66, 4.73]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "established[2]"], "text": "The 2023 and 2024 returns answer yes. One of those answers is wrong.", "t0": 58.78, "t1": 65.58, "shot": "d12", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "One of the answers is wrong"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.5, 1.22, 1.4, 1.73, 2.35, 3.19, 3.61, 4.94, 5.14, 5.2, 5.41, 6.18, 6.39]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "timeline[3]"], "text": "The third lead. For 2023, what pay does the return report for the President?", "t0": 65.8, "t1": 71.37, "shot": "d13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Form 990 for 2023", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "compensation reported for the President"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.48, 1.63, 1.79, 2.08, 2.78, 3.07, 3.37, 3.52, 3.63, 3.99, 4.32, 4.42, 4.52]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "links[3]"], "text": "507,817 dollars.", "t0": 71.37, "t1": 75.91, "shot": "d14", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$507,817", "label": "reported pay to the President, 2023", "sub": "44% of the year’s spending"}, "emph": ["507,817"], "wt": [0.04, 0.36, 1.14, 1.5, 2.63, 2.89, 3.45, 4.0]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[3]"], "text": "That’s 162,500 dollars of salary,", "t0": 76.43, "t1": 81.46, "shot": "d15", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["officer pay on the expense statement", "$162,500"], "b": ["paid to PJS", "$345,317"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.33, 0.6, 1.15, 2.27, 3.12, 3.44, 3.69, 4.01, 4.11]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[3]"], "text": "plus the payments to PJS.", "t0": 81.46, "t1": 83.5, "shot": "d15", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["officer pay on the expense statement", "$162,500"], "b": ["paid to PJS", "$345,317"]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.67, 0.81, 1.17, 1.28]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "share", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "Together, 44 percent of everything the charity spent that year.", "t0": 83.62, "t1": 87.28, "shot": "d16", "visual": {"type": "share", "pct": 44, "label": "of the year’s $1,166,439 of expenses"}, "emph": ["44 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.94, 1.48, 1.85, 2.0, 2.47, 2.57, 2.93, 3.19, 3.36]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[5]", "suspicious[2].what"], "text": "At City-paid organizations, the best-paid person’s median share is 3 percent.", "t0": 87.4, "t1": 91.34, "shot": "d17", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["best-paid person, City-paid organizations, median", "3%"], "b": ["this charity, 2023", "44%"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.57, 1.25, 1.4, 2.01, 2.44, 2.81, 3.14, 3.27, 3.48]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[5]"], "text": "Only 11 of 2,284 returns reach 44 percent or more.", "t0": 91.46, "t1": 95.75, "shot": "d17", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["best-paid person, City-paid organizations, median", "3%"], "b": ["this charity, 2023", "44%"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.33, 0.67, 0.76, 0.94, 1.29, 1.48, 1.71, 2.18, 2.82, 3.07, 3.55, 3.86, 3.96]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "story[3]"], "text": "The fourth lead: the City’s payment records. The first year’s title names the charity.", "t0": 95.97, "t1": 100.33, "shot": "d18", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "gvp", "kicker": "City payments, fiscal 2022", "text": "HRC-DKI-TA-006-BlackFemaleProj", "mark": "BlackFemaleProj"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.42, 0.92, 1.08, 1.43, 1.76, 2.5, 2.65, 2.9, 3.15, 3.49, 3.83, 3.93]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "links[0]"], "text": "From fiscal 2023, the title ends in “fsPJS”:", "t0": 100.45, "t1": 106.66, "shot": "d19", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["fiscal 2022", "HRC-DKI-TA-006-BlackFemaleProj"], "b": ["from fiscal 2023", "HRC-DKI-TA-006-BFP-fsPJS"], "kicker": "The same agreement, a new title"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.66, 1.01, 2.07, 2.23, 2.55, 2.79, 2.97, 3.32, 4.08, 4.8, 5.28]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "links[0]"], "text": "fiscal sponsor for PJS.", "t0": 106.66, "t1": 109.13, "shot": "d19", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["fiscal 2022", "HRC-DKI-TA-006-BlackFemaleProj"], "b": ["from fiscal 2023", "HRC-DKI-TA-006-BFP-fsPJS"], "kicker": "The same agreement, a new title"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.53, 1.54, 1.73, 1.93, 2.14]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["story[3]"], "text": "Fiscal sponsorship usually carries a charitable project. Here it appears to be the President’s own firm.", "t0": 109.25, "t1": 116.0, "shot": "d20", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "here the other party appears to be the President’s own consultancy"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.48, 1.3, 1.68, 2.11, 2.19, 2.64, 3.73, 4.52, 4.66, 5.05, 5.15, 5.26, 5.37, 5.92, 6.33]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "If the Commission knew, the charity was a channel for paying a private company.", "t0": 116.12, "t1": 119.67, "shot": "d21", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "the charity was a channel for a payment to a private company"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.24, 0.64, 1.29, 1.43, 1.81, 1.95, 2.02, 2.34, 2.48, 2.78, 2.84, 3.17]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "timeline[4]"], "text": "The fifth lead. The grant ended in June 2024.", "t0": 119.89, "t1": 123.7, "shot": "d22", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2024-06-30", "to": "2025-03-24", "days": "", "fromLab": "the agreement ends: $962,500 paid", "toLab": "the charity takes a new name", "kicker": "The fifth lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.64, 1.48, 1.65, 2.04, 2.3, 2.43, 2.81, 3.15]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "timeline[4]"], "text": "In March 2025, the charity renamed itself:", "t0": 123.82, "t1": 127.35, "shot": "d22", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2024-06-30", "to": "2025-03-24", "days": "", "fromLab": "the agreement ends: $962,500 paid", "toLab": "the charity takes a new name", "kicker": "The fifth lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.51, 0.77, 1.76, 1.9, 2.33, 2.73]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "actors[4]"], "text": "Qualitative Solutions, at the same Berkeley suite, in the President’s care.", "t0": 127.35, "t1": 131.62, "shot": "d23", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Qualitative Solutions", "kicker": "Renamed, 24 March 2025", "sub": "the same Berkeley suite, in the President’s care"}, "emph": ["Qualitative Solutions"], "wt": [0.04, 0.66, 1.56, 1.7, 1.84, 2.21, 2.58, 3.21, 3.36, 3.45, 3.92]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "timeline[5]"], "text": "Its 2025 return shows 20,026 dollars coming in. How much went out?", "t0": 131.74, "t1": 138.28, "shot": "d24", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["revenue, 2025", "$20,026"], "b": ["spending, 2025", "$334,712"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.51, 1.06, 1.63, 1.97, 2.24, 2.58, 3.05, 3.44, 3.74, 4.99, 5.19, 5.41, 5.59]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[4]", "timeline[5]"], "text": "334,712 dollars.", "t0": 138.28, "t1": 142.69, "shot": "d25", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$334,712", "label": "spent in 2025", "sub": "$52,244 left at the end of the year"}, "emph": ["334,712"], "wt": [0.04, 0.45, 0.8, 1.39, 2.44, 2.85, 3.27, 3.83]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "suspicious[4].why"], "text": "Of that, 172,313 dollars went to contractors the return doesn’t name.", "t0": 143.11, "t1": 150.09, "shot": "d26", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "$172,313", "label": "to contractors the short form does not name", "sub": "Form 990-EZ for 2025"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 1.1, 1.29, 1.67, 2.3, 2.78, 3.07, 3.44, 3.94, 4.72, 4.92, 5.02, 5.65, 5.77, 6.28, 6.63]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "innocent[0]", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "Nothing shows the work wasn’t done. The President may have done it through her own firm.", "t0": 150.31, "t1": 155.01, "shot": "d27", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That the technical assistance was not delivered", "What the Commission knew about PJS, and when", "Whether the board approved the payments to PJS"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.38, 0.84, 0.97, 1.2, 1.51, 2.29, 2.46, 2.97, 3.18, 3.31, 3.47, 3.64, 3.9, 4.06, 4.26]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? The Commission’s grant file, and the charity’s board minutes.", "t0": 155.13, "t1": 159.01, "shot": "d28", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The Commission’s grant file: invoices, deliverables, the “fsPJS” change"}, {"who": "", "what": "The charity’s board minutes approving the PJS payments"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.4, 0.71, 1.42, 1.55, 1.95, 2.2, 2.55, 2.69, 2.78, 3.24, 3.51]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "defense[0]"], "text": "We did not reach out to anyone in this film for comment. No regulator has ruled on the grant or the firm.", "t0": 159.13, "t1": 164.14, "shot": "d29", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.3, 0.5, 0.69, 0.84, 0.96, 1.28, 1.35, 1.52, 1.77, 1.9, 2.82, 3.07, 3.54, 3.68, 3.96, 4.04, 4.13, 4.4, 4.51, 4.61]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 164.26, "t1": 166.36, "shot": "d30", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.31, 0.4, 0.47, 1.18, 1.36, 1.45]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "Dream Keeper", "lead1": "Lead 1 · the President’s firm", "lead2": "Lead 2 · the 2022 return", "lead3": "Lead 3 · 44% of spending", "lead4": "Lead 4 · the City’s title", "lead5": "Lead 5 · renamed", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "newsroom", "hook": "person"}